# ── FriCAS on Windows (081M29N1AX9087G0R001GSJD6G) ─────────────────────────────────────────
#
# WHAT THIS ROW BUYS: a NATIVE Windows FriCAS. The brief that produced it assumed Windows
# would need WSL or Cygwin, as it historically did. Measured 2026-09-11, that is no longer
# true -- upstream publishes a self-contained Windows build, and since 1.3.13 it publishes one
# for arm64 too. So of the two computer-algebra systems asked for, only SageMath needs WSL;
# FriCAS does not, and saying which is which is the point of measuring rather than assuming.
#
# WHY from-zip AND NOT manifests/windows. scoop DOES carry fricas 1.3.13 -- but only in the
# Extras bucket, and `tools/setup/install.ps1` deliberately bootstraps Main alone (the same
# reason `wabt` is a WINDOWS_EXCEPTIONS entry rather than a scoop row). Adding a third-party
# bucket to reach a package whose bytes we would then pin by package-id only is strictly worse
# than naming the vendor's own asset and pinning its digest: a scoop row lands in the
# UNDECLARED half of docs/UNHASHED-DEPENDENCIES.md, these rows land in the digest-covered
# denominator.
#
# PINS IT: the two sha256 values below, each cross-checked against THREE independent
# publications, measured 2026-09-11:
#   x86-64  (1) upstream's own sha256sum-1.3.13.txt release asset,
#           (2) the GitHub release API's assets[].digest field,
#           (3) the ScoopInstaller/Extras bucket manifest's `hash`,
#           (4) and a fourth, weaker check: the bytes were downloaded and hashed here.
#   arm64   (2) and (4) only, stated rather than glossed -- the windows-arm64 asset was
#           uploaded 2026-07-09, four months AFTER the 1.3.13 sha256sum file was cut, so that
#           file does not cover it, and scoop's manifest carries no arm64 architecture block.
#
# NO `shim=`: the shim is a POSIX symlink, which is why the CodeQL win64 row above has none
# either. Windows callers use the path under <dest> or add it to PATH themselves.
#
# SIZE, STATED BECAUSE IT IS WHAT THE OPT-IN BUYS BACK: 35.7 MB (x86-64) / 37.4 MB (arm64)
# compressed. That is small for this mechanism -- and `opt-in=` is nonetheless MANDATORY here,
# by the realizer's own refusal, not by preference. NAMED PARITY DRIFT, GOVERNANCE §24: macOS
# and Linux get FriCAS automatically from brew/apt at tier=standard, Windows gets it only when
# ZETA_INSTALL_FRICAS=1. The mechanism that can unpack an archive is the mechanism that
# requires an opt-in, and `from-url` + `from-shim` -- the manifest's own advice for a small
# artifact -- cannot unpack. This is DEBT, not a design: closing it needs either a
# non-opt-in unpack mechanism or a Main-bucket scoop package, and both are separate decisions.
